<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 108 0 R
/T (Overall, the majority of immigrants across all timeframes rate their mental health positively. Meanwhile, the percentages of negative mental health ratings \(Fair and Poor\) remain relatively consistent across all groups. These results suggest that most immigrants report similar levels of positive and negative mental health regardless of how long they have been in the country.)
/E (Overall, the majority of immigrants across all timeframes rate their mental health positively. Meanwhile, the percentages of negative mental health ratings \(Fair and Poor\) remain relatively consistent across all groups. These results suggest that most immigrants report similar levels of positive and negative mental health regardless of how long they have been in the country.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
188 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 108 0 R
/T (According to a self-report screener, out of 4,142 participants, about half self-reported having experienced depression symptoms \(2,072\), and a slightly smaller number \(1,869\) reported anxiety symptoms. Fewer participants reported experiencing mania \(914\) or social phobia \(839\). Although immigrants rated their mental health positively overall, episodes of mental issues are still quite prevalent in the immigrant communities. Overall, depression and anxiety symptoms appear to be the most commonly reported mental health concerns.)
/E (According to a self-report screener, out of 4,142 participants, about half self-reported having experienced depression symptoms \(2,072\), and a slightly smaller number \(1,869\) reported anxiety symptoms. Fewer participants reported experiencing mania \(914\) or social phobia \(839\). Although immigrants rated their mental health positively overall, episodes of mental issues are still quite prevalent in the immigrant communities. Overall, depression and anxiety symptoms appear to be the most commonly reported mental health concerns.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
