194 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 108 0 R
/T (The actually diagnosed cases of mental disorders are relatively low, even though quite a significant number of immigrants reported experiencing symptoms. For example, about 50% of immigrants reported symptoms of depression, but only about 5% of them have a diagnosis. This is unlikely to be a case of massive under-diagnosis, because the majority of immigrants perceived their mental health condition as at least good. The more likely answer is that immigrants are facing quite some stress, but not bad enough to cause a formal diagnosis. This can be confirmed by looking at stress statistics we presented earlier. Over 50% of immigrants reported facing some level of life and work stress, and about 15% of them reported high levels of stress. As a result, mental health support for immigrants should focus on lessening general life and work stress, such as nutrition, sleep hygiene, social engagement, healthy life style.)
/E (The actually diagnosed cases of mental disorders are relatively low, even though quite a significant number of immigrants reported experiencing symptoms. For example, about 50% of immigrants reported symptoms of depression, but only about 5% of them have a diagnosis. This is unlikely to be a case of massive under-diagnosis, because the majority of immigrants perceived their mental health condition as at least good. The more likely answer is that immigrants are facing quite some stress, but not bad enough to cause a formal diagnosis. This can be confirmed by looking at stress statistics we presented earlier. Over 50% of immigrants reported facing some level of life and work stress, and about 15% of them reported high levels of stress. As a result, mental health support for immigrants should focus on lessening general life and work stress, such as nutrition, sleep hygiene, social engagement, healthy life style.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
