462 0 obj
<<
/Title (Immigrating to a new country is a transformative experience that brings both opportunities and challenges. Mental health plays a crucial role in how individuals adapt to life in Canada, yet many newcomers may face stress, isolation, or uncertainty during their transition. This poster uses data from Statistics Canada to provide clear, accessible insights into the mental health experiences of immigrants in Canada. By presenting this information in an easy-to-understand format, we aim to empower newcomers with knowledge, reduce stigma, and encourage engagement with the community.)
/Dest [9 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 421 0 R
>>
endobj
